From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: cloud storage in Settings and Files, through rclone

nickel-cloud keeps the user's cloud storage accounts (Google Drive,
OneDrive, Dropbox, Proton Drive, Box, pCloud, S3, Nextcloud/WebDAV) with
rclone and mounts each one under $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nickel-cloud/drives.
Its D-Bus service, org.nickelos.Cloud on the session bus, is what Chrome
talks to (file_manager::NickelCloudClient, a private connection to
/run/user/<uid>/bus on its own thread):

- Files: VolumeManager adds each mounted account as a volume of the new
  type nickel_cloud (VOLUME_TYPE_NICKEL_CLOUD, RootType.NICKEL_CLOUD),
  shown in the sidebar's cloud section with a cloud icon, and follows
  nickel-cloud's Changed signal. Files can't unmount these: the accounts
  are managed in Settings. The folder tree scans their folders as it does
  local ones (rclone keeps the listings), so only folders with folders in
  them get an expand arrow.
- Settings > System preferences > Files > Cloud storage: the accounts with
  their state, Add account and Remove. The add dialog (nickel-cloud-dialog)
  asks for the service and what it needs (Google Drive: the user's own
  client ID and secret), then answers rclone's configuration one question
  at a time; services that sign in through their web page open it in the
  browser, and the dialog waits for it. NickelCloudHandler passes the
  calls on.

